                <pb facs="0540" n="438" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg438"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister for Foreign Affairs to Minister
                        Furniss.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port au
                                Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-05-20"><hi rendition="#italic">May 20,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 113.]</seg></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: With a view of putting an end to
                    the custom—only too much abused—of asylum in the legations and consulates
                    established in Haiti, my department has just notified the diplomatic corps in
                    this city of the decision that the Haitian Government has deemed necessary to
                    take relative thereto, and of which I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy
                    for the information of your excellency.</p>
                <p>I take, with pleasure, this occasion to renew to you, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Louis Borno.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
